          },
          "blocks": {
            "accordion_row_NTr3Di": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What's the difference between The Hippie Pipe, Pipe X, and OM Chrome?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_TPb9Kx": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>All three share the same core analog, telescopic mechanism. Pipe X adds a darker, blacked-out finish, OM Chrome steps up with a ~30% bigger chamber and a rapid-convection airpath for a smoother draw.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "max_width_custom": 600,
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_TPb9Kx"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_VUdFGK": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "Are your devices electronic or manual?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_3nnat8": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>The Hippie Pipe, Pipe X, and OM Chrome are 100% analog, no battery, no charging, torch-powered. OM Gunmetal and OM Rose Gold are rechargeable 510-thread batteries built for compatible atomizers.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "max_width_custom": 600,
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_3nnat8"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_wbtt8f": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What's the difference between OM Gunmetal and OM Rose Gold?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_YhLaYt": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Both are rechargeable 510-thread batteries on the same platform. OM Gunmetal has a mirror finish, OM Rose Gold adds a rose gold finish and a longer protective cap over the threading.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "max_width_custom": 600,
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_YhLaYt"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_rNkU8V": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "What is a 510-thread battery, and how do I charge it?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_k3YxRW": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>510 is the industry-standard threading that connects a battery to compatible atomizers. Charge OM Gunmetal or OM Rose Gold with the included cable before first use, an LED indicator signals when charging is complete.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "max_width_custom": 600,
                    "alignment": "left",
                    "type_preset": "rte",
                    "font": "var(--font-body--family)",
                    "font_size": "1rem",
                    "line_height": "normal",
                    "letter_spacing": "normal",
                    "case": "none",
                    "wrap": "pretty",
                    "text_color": "",
                    "background": false,
                    "background_color": "#00000026",
                    "corner_radius": 0,
                    "padding-block-start": 0,
                    "padding-block-end": 0,
                    "padding-inline-start": 0,
                    "padding-inline-end": 0
                  },
                  "blocks": {}
                }
              },
              "block_order": [
                "text_k3YxRW"
              ]
            },
            "accordion_row_b7bQYE": {
              "type": "_accordion-row",
              "name": "t:names.accordion_row",
              "settings": {
                "heading": "How do I clean and maintain my device?",
                "open_by_default": false,
                "icon": "none",
                "width": 20
              },
              "blocks": {
                "text_8maxJ4": {
                  "type": "text",
                  "settings": {
                    "text": "<p>Let it cool, then wipe the chamber with a cotton swab or pipe cleaner and swap the screen when airflow feels restricted. For battery devices, wipe the exterior with a dry or slightly damp cloth, never submerge components in water.</p>",
                    "width": "100%",
                    "max_width": "none",
                    "max_width_custom": 600,
                    "alignment": "left",
